WEBVTT

00:00:01.430 --> 00:00:05.900
Sanriio Military Academy

00:00:02.620 --> 00:00:05.310
<i>The prestigious Sanriio Military Academy</i>.

00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:11.240
<i>Here, young people learn together and foster
friendships that transcend nationalities.</i>

00:00:12.010 --> 00:00:12.810
<i>However—</i>

00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:18.660
<b>Shuun, Cinnaamoll Empire Knight Candidate</b>

00:00:14.110 --> 00:00:18.660
I've always wanted to fight
you seriously, Yuucisus.

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:22.540
And I would've preferred to not have
to deal with you when you're so serious.

00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:22.540
<b>Yuucisus, Kikiira Kingdom Knight Candidate</b>

00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:27.960
<i>The premonition of war that
spread through the various nations</i>

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:30.960
<i>also created rifts in the
friendships of the students.</i>

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:32.740
Sei! Riyon!

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:35.310
Please stop them!

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:38.470
<b>Koural, Pomrin Duchy Nobleman</b>

00:00:35.310 --> 00:00:38.470
We may be from different countries,
but we're friends, aren't we?!

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:44.480
<b>Prince Sei, Cinnaamoll Empire</b>

00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:44.480
I'm sorry. As a prince of the
empire, I cannot stop Yuucisus.

00:00:44.730 --> 00:00:49.980
<b>Prince Riyon, Kikiira Kingdom</b>

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:45.930
I cannot either.

00:00:46.410 --> 00:00:49.980
The dignity of the motherland 
rests on this duel.

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:52.530
No way! There are things more important than—

00:00:52.530 --> 00:00:53.690
Don't say it, Koural!

00:00:53.690 --> 00:00:55.360
Please, don't say anymore.

00:00:56.900 --> 00:00:58.810
Sei, Riyon...

00:01:00.230 --> 00:01:02.390
Let's put an end to this.

00:01:02.390 --> 00:01:04.730
Right. I'll be the victor.

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:05.840
Nonsense.

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:12.170
Stop!

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:24.810
Koural!

00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:28.430
Koural, why would you do something like that?!

00:01:28.430 --> 00:01:30.150
You idiot...!

00:01:30.150 --> 00:01:32.490
Hang in there! Please hang in there!

00:01:32.490 --> 00:01:34.400
Hold on, I'll summon the doctor immediately!

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:40.420
Koural!

00:01:40.910 --> 00:01:43.830
Koural!

00:01:44.780 --> 00:01:46.040
<i>Oh, I'm fine!</i>

00:01:46.670 --> 00:01:47.870
<i>This is just a play.</i>

00:01:56.510 --> 00:02:01.760
<i>You can look forward to seeing
how things got to this point.</i>

00:01:59.220 --> 00:02:02.720
<b>Hijirikawa High School Cultural Festival</b>

00:02:03.310 --> 00:02:05.900
<i>Now, let's get started everyone.</i>

00:02:06.980 --> 00:02:09.230
<b>Mizuno Yuu</b>

00:02:07.450 --> 00:02:08.640
Mizuno Yuu.

00:02:09.980 --> 00:02:12.230
<b>Yoshino Shunsuke</b>

00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:11.760
Yoshino Shunsuke.

00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:15.230
<b>Nishimiya Ryo</b>

00:02:13.480 --> 00:02:14.810
Nishimiya Ryo.

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:18.240
<b>Minamoto Seiichirou</b>

00:02:16.450 --> 00:02:18.020
Minamoto Seiichirou.

00:02:19.690 --> 00:02:22.240
And I'm the one who was just stabbed to death,

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:24.490
<b>Hasegawa Kouta</b>

00:02:22.710 --> 00:02:23.860
Hasegawa Kouta.

00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:27.490
This is...

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:30.860
...the story of how "I" became "us".

00:02:38.460 --> 00:02:42.150
<i>This was still before any of us had met.</i>

00:02:53.610 --> 00:02:55.660
Ow...

00:02:58.630 --> 00:03:01.490
Kouta! Breakfast is ready!

00:03:01.880 --> 00:03:03.620
Okay.

00:03:04.900 --> 00:03:06.250
I'm off.

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:11.920
It All Started With Pompompurin

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:12.960
<i>I, Hasegawa Kouta, am a completely normal
and average second-year high school student,</i>

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:15.640
<i>even if I do say so myself.</i>

00:03:16.750 --> 00:03:19.500
<i>Though when I started going here a year ago</i>

00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:22.480
<i>I thought I was shining brightly.</i>

00:03:24.510 --> 00:03:28.840
<i>But in front of the wall
separating dreams and reality,</i>

00:03:28.840 --> 00:03:32.380
<i>such a small sparkle winds up fading.</i>

00:03:33.410 --> 00:03:35.060
Good morning.

00:03:34.260 --> 00:03:35.060
Morning.

00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:38.200
Good morning, President Minamoto.

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:39.820
Yes, good morning.

00:03:39.820 --> 00:03:41.870
You've got bags under your eyes.

00:03:41.870 --> 00:03:45.350
If you keep studying too much, it will
have the opposite effect on your grades.

00:03:46.610 --> 00:03:47.410
Morning.

00:03:48.140 --> 00:03:49.780
G-Good morning.

00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:55.700
Try to fix your bed head
before going to class.

00:04:17.210 --> 00:04:21.120
<i>It's not like I'm necessarily
unhappy with my life right now.</i>

00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:22.540
<i>But...</i>

00:04:23.340 --> 00:04:28.220
<i>But when I look at those around
me who are shining now...</i>

00:04:28.550 --> 00:04:32.910
<i>I wonder if my youth is shining
in the same way, too.</i>

00:04:36.070 --> 00:04:39.040
<i>Or, so I thought.</i>

00:04:41.170 --> 00:04:42.670
I'm being totally serious.

00:04:44.120 --> 00:04:46.450
<i>It's probably hopeless for me after all.</i>

00:04:46.450 --> 00:04:49.390
Sorry for keeping you, Hase.

00:04:49.390 --> 00:04:52.070
No worries. I hope you had a
good baseball practice, Tsucchi.

00:04:53.740 --> 00:04:55.120
What's the matter, Macchi?

00:04:55.120 --> 00:04:57.740
Isn't that Mizuno from Class 4?! Damn it!

00:04:57.740 --> 00:05:01.120
How is someone not in any clubs more
popular than me in the light music club?!

00:05:03.690 --> 00:05:06.030
Hey, he's just asking for a fight!

00:05:06.030 --> 00:05:07.990
Smiling like that?

00:05:07.990 --> 00:05:10.560
It's difficult for people
to understand each other.

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:13.300
Damn it! What the heck!

00:05:10.990 --> 00:05:13.700
Which reminds me, Hase,
you seemed to be spacing out a bit,

00:05:13.300 --> 00:05:16.200
I really hate good-looking guys!

00:05:13.700 --> 00:05:15.430
something on your mind?

00:05:16.410 --> 00:05:18.380
Oh, well, more than thinking—

00:05:18.870 --> 00:05:20.080
Don't finish that thought.

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:23.150
I understand everything about you, my friend.

00:05:23.980 --> 00:05:27.090
You want a girlfriend, right?

00:05:29.420 --> 00:05:31.520
Amazing, Macchi is the only
one who can make Hase,

00:05:31.520 --> 00:05:33.770
who accepts just about
anything, make that face.

00:05:33.770 --> 00:05:35.330
Stop it, you're making me blush!

00:05:35.330 --> 00:05:40.690
Which means we should all
go out looking for girls this Sunday!

00:05:38.950 --> 00:05:40.690
Sorry, I have a girlfriend.

00:05:42.690 --> 00:05:44.660
You won't betray me, will you, Hase?!

00:05:44.660 --> 00:05:48.010
You definitely, definitely,
definitely won't betray me, right?!

00:05:46.490 --> 00:05:49.050
So, the three of us will be hanging out, then.

00:05:49.050 --> 00:05:51.830
We can meet up in front
of the station at 11 o'clock, right?

00:05:51.830 --> 00:05:53.270
I want a girlfriend!

00:05:53.270 --> 00:05:56.110
I want a tanned gal girlfriend!

00:06:00.230 --> 00:06:01.550
Was that...

00:06:01.550 --> 00:06:03.710
Are you listening to me?! I really want one!

00:06:03.710 --> 00:06:06.220
<b>Sunday</b>

00:06:22.060 --> 00:06:23.070
<b>Karaoke</b>

00:06:27.390 --> 00:06:29.080
I feel so much better!

00:06:29.500 --> 00:06:32.060
Not surprising since you sang so loud.

00:06:32.640 --> 00:06:34.260
What's the matter, Hase?

00:06:34.600 --> 00:06:37.890
Well, uh, it's just her...

00:06:39.070 --> 00:06:42.040
Mommy, where are you?

00:06:39.450 --> 00:06:41.000
She must be lost.

00:06:41.420 --> 00:06:42.300
Looks like it.

00:06:44.560 --> 00:06:47.380
So what? Her parents will find her eventually.

00:06:47.380 --> 00:06:48.840
Anyway, where should we go next?

00:06:49.230 --> 00:06:50.120
Yeah...

00:06:50.120 --> 00:06:51.510
Just forget it.

00:06:51.510 --> 00:06:55.320
In this day and age, if you try to talk
to her, you're just going to get reported.

00:06:56.190 --> 00:07:00.220
That's true, it might wind up
just being a huge mess.

00:07:07.510 --> 00:07:09.260
Sorry, I'm going to go anyway!

00:07:09.260 --> 00:07:10.110
Hey, Hase!

00:07:13.960 --> 00:07:16.350
Will you vouch for me if I get caught?

00:07:16.350 --> 00:07:17.150
Such a softy.

00:07:17.150 --> 00:07:18.950
We get, if you're gonna go, go already.

00:07:19.610 --> 00:07:21.210
Um...

00:07:21.790 --> 00:07:24.030
Did you come here today with your mom?

00:07:24.910 --> 00:07:26.900
Mommy!

00:07:45.740 --> 00:07:48.230
Oh, this is really cute! So you like Pom—

00:07:49.740 --> 00:07:52.140
Puppies, huh?

00:07:55.960 --> 00:07:58.850
I like... Pompompurin...

00:07:59.510 --> 00:08:02.620
Okay, so he's called Pompompurin.

00:08:03.340 --> 00:08:05.170
He's all puffy and cute, isn't he?

00:08:08.820 --> 00:08:09.800
His butt...

00:08:11.510 --> 00:08:14.090
<b>Factoid: Pompompurin's most attractive feature is his "butt hole".</b>

00:08:15.710 --> 00:08:17.450
You're right. It's his butt.

00:08:17.900 --> 00:08:19.980
And poke, poke.

00:08:21.570 --> 00:08:22.620
Poke, poke.

00:08:24.060 --> 00:08:26.980
Poke, poke. Butt.

00:08:25.010 --> 00:08:25.850
<i>There</i>?

00:08:32.970 --> 00:08:34.280
I have tissues.

00:08:35.100 --> 00:08:36.310
Oh, oops.

00:08:37.700 --> 00:08:39.660
This is...

00:08:39.660 --> 00:08:42.490
<b>Lost Child Card
Name: Satou Mana
Guardian Contact Number:</b>

00:08:40.460 --> 00:08:42.940
Yes! This'll work...

00:08:44.930 --> 00:08:47.100
Thank you so much.

00:08:48.540 --> 00:08:50.800
Thank you, Onii-chan.

00:08:50.800 --> 00:08:52.360
You're welcome.

00:08:54.420 --> 00:08:55.580
I want to give you this!

00:08:55.580 --> 00:08:57.320
A-Are you sure?

00:08:57.320 --> 00:08:58.120
Yeah!

00:08:58.800 --> 00:09:02.310
Well then, thank you.

00:09:04.620 --> 00:09:07.120
Bye-bye, Onii-chan!

00:09:08.780 --> 00:09:11.730
Jeez, you're such a nice guy.

00:09:11.730 --> 00:09:14.060
Made it out without a criminal history, Hase.

00:09:14.060 --> 00:09:17.480
Tsucchi, you would've vouched for me, right?

00:09:18.130 --> 00:09:20.010
What did you she give you anyway?

00:09:20.430 --> 00:09:22.040
Oh, this?

00:09:22.560 --> 00:09:24.930
What's this? Some kind of new steamed bun?

00:09:24.930 --> 00:09:29.680
Oh this, he's one of those Sanrio
characters just like Hello Kitty.

00:09:29.680 --> 00:09:31.100
That brings back memories.

00:09:31.100 --> 00:09:34.720
I think I had something of it as a
kid, what was its name again...

00:09:35.710 --> 00:09:38.400
She said it was called Pompompurin.

00:09:38.400 --> 00:09:42.810
Still, it'd be pretty weird for a high school guy
to have something like that though.

00:09:43.130 --> 00:09:44.730
Oh, yeah...

00:09:45.120 --> 00:09:47.570
You're... right.

00:09:48.110 --> 00:09:51.100
But it might make you pretty
popular with little girls.

00:09:51.100 --> 00:09:52.660
Police officer!

00:09:52.660 --> 00:09:55.440
Wait, my friend! You're joking, right?!

00:10:00.810 --> 00:10:02.380
What's the matter?

00:10:02.380 --> 00:10:05.780
Didn't you hang out with your friends
today? Did something happen?

00:10:05.780 --> 00:10:08.590
Or is it a problem at school?

00:10:08.590 --> 00:10:09.290
Huh?

00:10:09.780 --> 00:10:10.770
No,

00:10:11.410 --> 00:10:15.260
hanging out with Tsucchi and Macchi
was fun and so is going to school.

00:10:15.930 --> 00:10:18.260
Or, it should be fun...

00:10:19.110 --> 00:10:22.600
Something feels like it's missing, though...

00:10:23.340 --> 00:10:25.350
Sorry, I can't really explain it.

00:10:26.420 --> 00:10:29.650
In other words, despite
moving up to second-year,

00:10:29.650 --> 00:10:33.020
nothing has changed in your life, is that it?

00:10:33.360 --> 00:10:36.810
It's because you don't have any
extracurricular activities or lessons, Kouta.

00:10:37.430 --> 00:10:40.750
I know, what if you went to prep school—

00:10:40.750 --> 00:10:42.780
I'm fine! I'm totally fine!

00:10:45.110 --> 00:10:49.550
If that's the case, then why don't
you try to accomplish something?

00:10:50.230 --> 00:10:53.070
Accomplish what though?

00:10:53.070 --> 00:10:56.000
Whatever you feel like you might want to do.

00:10:56.690 --> 00:10:58.660
Once you accomplish
something you've set your mind to,

00:10:58.660 --> 00:11:01.960
the sense of accomplishment is intoxicating.

00:11:08.200 --> 00:11:11.640
Accomplish something I want to do, huh?

00:11:12.830 --> 00:11:15.320
I can't just find something
like that out of the blue.

00:11:15.630 --> 00:11:18.150
Besides, even if I did find
something like that...

00:11:22.090 --> 00:11:24.760
It's hopeless for someone
like me who doesn't shine...

00:11:35.500 --> 00:11:38.140
Pompompurin, huh?

00:11:39.680 --> 00:11:44.260
<i>There is nothing you can't do, Kou-chan</i>.

00:11:52.960 --> 00:11:55.460
It's been four years, hasn't it?

00:11:56.670 --> 00:11:59.410
<i>It's all right, you can do it</i>.

00:11:59.410 --> 00:12:03.390
<i>Look, Purin and I will watch you together</i>.

00:12:08.790 --> 00:12:11.460
Just a little more, Kou-chan!

00:12:11.890 --> 00:12:14.330
Purin is cheering you on, too.

00:12:27.260 --> 00:12:28.470
I did it!

00:12:28.770 --> 00:12:30.730
Grandma, I did it!

00:12:32.490 --> 00:12:34.980
<i>My grandma always believed
in me, no matter what,</i>

00:12:35.660 --> 00:12:40.120
<i>and she was my biggest supporter.</i>

00:12:42.220 --> 00:12:47.710
<i>I loved my grandma and the
Pompompurin she gave me.</i>

00:12:49.790 --> 00:12:52.250
<i>Everywhere I went, everything I did,</i>

00:12:52.970 --> 00:12:54.780
<i>I had my grandma and Purin with me.</i>

00:12:55.490 --> 00:12:59.780
<i>I thought that was how
things would always be.</i>

00:13:00.670 --> 00:13:04.260
You should be embarrassed
liking stuffed animals like that.

00:13:04.620 --> 00:13:06.760
It's like Kouta's a girl!

00:13:06.760 --> 00:13:10.210
Girl, girl, Kouta's a girl!

00:13:10.210 --> 00:13:11.840
He's Koutako, Koutako!

00:13:11.840 --> 00:13:13.610
I'm not a girl!

00:13:13.610 --> 00:13:15.200
You jerks!

00:13:15.200 --> 00:13:17.520
We made Kouta mad, run!

00:13:17.520 --> 00:13:21.720
Stupid! Idiots! Pieces of crap!

00:13:28.250 --> 00:13:30.520
Oh, dear. How awful.

00:13:31.110 --> 00:13:34.620
You've gotten so dirty, Purin-chan.

00:13:35.170 --> 00:13:38.150
Oh, my. You've hurt your ear.

00:13:40.330 --> 00:13:44.670
It'll be all right, Kou-chan.
I'll fix him up for you.

00:13:44.670 --> 00:13:48.130
I don't care. I don't need
such a girly thing anymore.

00:13:49.290 --> 00:13:53.070
But I should fix him anyway, the poor thing...

00:13:53.070 --> 00:13:53.900
Shut up!

00:13:54.890 --> 00:13:59.050
I hate Pompompurin and you, Grandma!

00:14:02.890 --> 00:14:07.980
<i>After that, I stayed away from my grandma.</i>

00:14:09.260 --> 00:14:13.570
<i>Now that I think about it, that was
probably the start of my rebellious phase.</i>

00:14:17.620 --> 00:14:19.600
It's all right.

00:14:19.600 --> 00:14:24.330
Kou-chan is a sweet child,
he'll come to see us soon, I'm sure.

00:14:29.370 --> 00:14:36.100
<i>Even so, it would take a bit
longer for me to be honest</i>

00:14:35.770 --> 00:14:39.100
<b>Hospital</b>

00:14:36.100 --> 00:14:39.100
<i>with my grandma who never
stopped caring for me.</i>

00:14:47.710 --> 00:14:51.030
Tomorrow. I'll definitely
talk to her tomorrow.

00:14:52.110 --> 00:14:53.780
<i>If I just apologized to her,</i>

00:14:54.390 --> 00:14:58.160
<i>then we could be together
like we'd always been.</i>

00:15:00.350 --> 00:15:03.500
<i>I completely believed that.</i>

00:15:46.330 --> 00:15:47.890
<i>I never doubted it.</i>

00:15:54.140 --> 00:15:55.280
Grandma...

00:15:56.010 --> 00:15:58.510
You said I could do anything, right?

00:15:59.320 --> 00:16:01.550
But, it's hopeless.

00:16:02.410 --> 00:16:06.860
I wasn't able to apologize and I can't
even admit to liking the things that I like.

00:16:08.000 --> 00:16:09.170
I'm hopeless...

00:16:12.280 --> 00:16:14.280
<b>Showers</b>

00:16:19.000 --> 00:16:19.940
Heya.

00:16:21.610 --> 00:16:23.250
Good job in practice this morning.

00:16:23.250 --> 00:16:25.580
The hell, Yuu? Don't look.

00:16:25.580 --> 00:16:26.960
A little late for that.

00:16:26.960 --> 00:16:30.300
We're friends who already know all
the embarrassing parts of each other, right?

00:16:30.300 --> 00:16:32.050
Knock it off. Go away.

00:16:32.620 --> 00:16:34.800
I noticed something this morning.

00:16:35.360 --> 00:16:39.810
Apparently, one of my princesses
has gone missing all of the sudden.

00:16:40.370 --> 00:16:43.160
Shunsuke, you had club
activities all weekend, right?

00:16:43.160 --> 00:16:44.920
Did you see her somewhere?

00:16:45.290 --> 00:16:47.670
I'm sure she's feeling so alone by herself.

00:16:47.670 --> 00:16:50.070
Like I'd know? She was going
to leave eventually.

00:16:50.070 --> 00:16:52.640
You're so mean, Shushu!

00:16:52.640 --> 00:16:54.010
Get out of here already.

00:17:00.410 --> 00:17:01.610
This is...

00:17:03.100 --> 00:17:05.090
My Melody, isn't it?

00:17:05.890 --> 00:17:09.040
I'm pretty sure...

00:17:09.040 --> 00:17:12.420
Yuu

00:17:09.040 --> 00:17:12.420
Shushu

00:17:09.520 --> 00:17:12.420
this is Mizuno from class 4, isn't it?

00:17:14.460 --> 00:17:17.350
<i>So I didn't mistake what I saw after all.</i>

00:17:18.540 --> 00:17:22.570
<i>He uses Sanrio merchandise
even though he's so gaudy.</i>

00:17:23.390 --> 00:17:25.620
<i>I'll give it to him during break.</i>

00:17:27.290 --> 00:17:28.410
Got a minute?

00:17:28.770 --> 00:17:31.270
Mizuno-kun is in this class, isn't he?

00:17:31.270 --> 00:17:32.450
Yeah, he is.

00:17:32.990 --> 00:17:35.540
Hey, Mizuno!

00:17:34.030 --> 00:17:35.540
It's a new flavor...

00:17:36.730 --> 00:17:37.530
You called?

00:17:37.530 --> 00:17:38.640
You have a guest.

00:17:40.030 --> 00:17:43.050
Um... aren't you from the neighboring class?

00:17:43.050 --> 00:17:44.870
Oh, I'm Hasegawa Kouta.

00:17:44.870 --> 00:17:47.070
That's right, Hasegawa, Hasegawa.

00:17:47.070 --> 00:17:47.920
So, what's up?

00:17:48.270 --> 00:17:50.170
Well, I have this...

00:17:50.170 --> 00:17:51.880
Yuu, are you done yet?

00:17:53.700 --> 00:17:54.550
What's the matter?

00:17:54.860 --> 00:17:56.840
<i>Wait... I gotta wait a second.</i>

00:17:57.210 --> 00:17:59.800
<i>If I give this to him now...</i>

00:17:59.800 --> 00:18:03.660
What? Yuu uses that kind
of thing even though he's a guy?

00:18:03.660 --> 00:18:04.930
Ugh, how gross.

00:18:05.210 --> 00:18:06.060
<i>I can't!</i>

00:18:06.060 --> 00:18:08.060
S-Sorry, it's nothing!

00:18:08.750 --> 00:18:10.150
Hey, wait!

00:18:11.950 --> 00:18:13.040
That's...

00:18:15.370 --> 00:18:16.570
Wait a minute!

00:18:16.780 --> 00:18:18.610
<i>Ugh, I'm such an idiot!</i>

00:18:19.610 --> 00:18:21.490
<i>I gotta pay more attention!</i>

00:18:26.270 --> 00:18:27.380
Are you okay?

00:18:30.270 --> 00:18:32.880
Sorry! I'm kind of in a hurry!

00:18:36.510 --> 00:18:38.660
Hey, why are you running away?

00:18:38.660 --> 00:18:40.720
Well, I'm sorry about a bunch of things!

00:18:41.000 --> 00:18:43.640
It kinda hurts my feelings that
you're running away though!

00:18:43.640 --> 00:18:45.930
That's why I said I'm really sorry!

00:18:49.130 --> 00:18:50.230
How stupid.

00:18:50.230 --> 00:18:54.040
Oh, but it's pretty fun running like this!

00:18:54.040 --> 00:18:55.230
It's a positive thing?!

00:18:59.650 --> 00:19:01.360
You two, stop!

00:19:03.570 --> 00:19:05.040
Don't run in the halls.

00:19:05.490 --> 00:19:07.820
You don't want to get hurt
or hurt anyone, do you?

00:19:07.820 --> 00:19:09.410
No, president!

00:19:09.790 --> 00:19:10.590
Okay then.

00:19:23.550 --> 00:19:26.240
You bad boy. You should listen
to the president's orders!

00:19:26.240 --> 00:19:27.430
You should, too!

00:19:27.430 --> 00:19:31.140
Jeez, where did that
idiot Yuu drop that thing?

00:19:31.140 --> 00:19:32.570
Wait up!

00:19:35.310 --> 00:19:36.360
Yuu?

00:19:37.340 --> 00:19:39.480
That's weird.

00:19:39.480 --> 00:19:42.110
I thought he went this way.

00:19:52.880 --> 00:19:54.660
I think I lost him.

00:19:56.870 --> 00:19:58.170
I'm sorry, Mizuno.

00:20:00.730 --> 00:20:04.510
I can't let you go through
something like that because of me.

00:20:05.080 --> 00:20:06.530
Because of me, what?

00:20:06.900 --> 00:20:07.510
Huh?

00:20:13.170 --> 00:20:14.400
Yoshino?

00:20:14.400 --> 00:20:16.400
Did you do something to him?

00:20:17.160 --> 00:20:19.030
No way, I—

00:20:19.030 --> 00:20:20.610
You, what?

00:20:24.910 --> 00:20:27.030
Okay, that's enough.

00:20:27.660 --> 00:20:30.540
He was just trying to return this to me.

00:20:31.050 --> 00:20:33.340
My adorable princess.

00:20:34.810 --> 00:20:36.330
Thank you, Hasegawa.

00:20:36.720 --> 00:20:38.780
And you, too, Shushu.

00:20:38.780 --> 00:20:40.300
That was misleading.

00:20:40.860 --> 00:20:43.820
So, why were you running?

00:20:45.630 --> 00:20:47.630
W-Well...

00:20:47.630 --> 00:20:48.600
Huh?

00:20:48.860 --> 00:20:51.380
What're you doing here, Yuu?

00:20:51.380 --> 00:20:53.100
Yoshino-kun, too.

00:20:54.060 --> 00:20:55.810
That thing you're holding, Yuu...

00:20:58.980 --> 00:21:02.250
So, you really like Sanrio, huh?

00:21:02.250 --> 00:21:03.380
No kidding.

00:21:03.820 --> 00:21:06.150
She's so cute though.

00:21:06.150 --> 00:21:07.660
She's my My Melody-chan.

00:21:08.830 --> 00:21:09.830
Wha?!

00:21:10.040 --> 00:21:12.810
Well, she is pretty cute...

00:21:12.810 --> 00:21:17.030
But it's kinda weird for a guy to
have something like that, right?

00:21:17.030 --> 00:21:18.710
That's not true.

00:21:19.200 --> 00:21:20.710
Right, Shunsuke?

00:21:20.710 --> 00:21:22.360
Don't get me involved.

00:21:25.050 --> 00:21:28.380
Look, even Shushu likes Hello Kitty-chan.

00:21:28.380 --> 00:21:31.000
It's not "chan", it's Hello Kitty-san.

00:21:31.000 --> 00:21:32.020
Well,

00:21:32.550 --> 00:21:36.920
I guess you could say we're the Sanrio Boys.

00:21:39.790 --> 00:21:42.730
Sanrio Boys...?

00:21:43.660 --> 00:21:46.550
<i>I'm pretty sure this was the moment.</i>

00:21:47.390 --> 00:21:50.130
<i>The moment that my youth began to be colored</i>

00:21:50.130 --> 00:21:53.360
<i>by a shining light that it didn't have before.</i>

00:21:55.080 --> 00:21:57.910
<i>Our story begins.</i>

00:23:33.110 --> 00:23:33.910
Huh?

00:23:34.850 --> 00:23:39.770
Next Episode

00:23:36.320 --> 00:23:39.090
Next time, "Gift Gate After the Rain."
